<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Balkan Wars</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1912–1913</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Balkan Wars were two wars fought in 1912–1913 in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>. In the first, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> and Montenegro defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> and took almost all its remaining European territory. In the second, the victors fought among themselves, and the conflicts heightened tensions before the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/balkan-wars.jpg" alt="Balkan Wars" width="320" height="206" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Luleburgaz_Battle_Postcard.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
